{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head f6aa8537b1bcbd0e72865214c90205797f2ac2a6, tree a667f460, on builder/as2-archive-stop-cause-20261117, all 8 artifacts, for request 8ed7cd50 under my promise aa49fbd4. This verdict names the one implementation: AS-2 (request 5443b484, promise d9dcb9ab, report `packages/scope/src/archive-budget.ts`, primary). Its parent is main 830d134a. LC-5 has since landed as ed2aaba1, and the two heads change no path in common.\n\n## First: retry and wake behaviour do not change\n\nThe ruling in ff12d4f2 allows no change to retry or wake behaviour. I read each changed line against that condition:\n\n- `ArchiveBudget.stop()` takes a third, optional `cause`. It stores the cause only when no stop has happened yet. The rest of the method is unchanged: `this.#stopped ??= reason`, then it throws the same `ArchiveStopped` with the same reason and refusal.\n- `check()` still stops as `unavailable` for a clock that is not finite or runs backwards. It now passes the clock cause. The `timeout` stop and the lookahead throw are unchanged.\n- The catch in `wait()` still rethrows a budget stop, still runs `check()` when the lookahead is blocked, and still stops as `unavailable`. It now passes the wait cause.\n- `sendArchiveAppend` still stops on the same three verifier reasons and still throws `bad()`. It now passes the verifier cause.\n- `archive-driver.ts` adds one field, `stopCause`, to the diagnostic record inside the existing `try { … } catch {}`. A failure there cannot change the pass result. The row, `#retryWake`, `#later` and the stored wake are untouched.\n\nSo the wake rate stays where AR-1 set it: a floor of 60 s between retries, doubling up to a one-hour cap, with a persisted retry count. The head adds no alarm, wake or request. The LC-5 deployment rate read is the baseline for the AS-2 deployment.\n\n## Security\n\nThe log holds names only. `archiveStopName` accepts a letter followed by up to 63 letters, digits, `_` or `-`. Anything else 